---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTABlock from '../../components/CTABlock.astro';
import { ROUTES } from '../../i18n/routes';
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  active="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy — Villa Solmira"
  description="How Villa Solmira handles your personal data when you send a booking or contact request."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap page-intro">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: 18 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap legal">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Villa Solmira is rented out by Evelien Deschuytter and Jurgen Bervoet, Solana 15,
        Hondón de las Nieves, Spain. For questions about this privacy policy or your data, you
        can reach us at info@villa-solmira.eu.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
      <p>Via the booking and contact form on this website, we collect:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>Name</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Phone number (on a booking request, optional)</li>
        <li>Desired arrival and departure dates and number of guests (on a booking request)</li>
        <li>The content of your message</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This site also uses a few cookies, Google Analytics and an external map service — see
        "Cookies" and
        "Sharing with third parties" below for the full picture.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Why we collect this data</h2>
      <p>
        We use this data solely to respond to your request, process a booking, and communicate
        about your stay. We don't use your data for marketing purposes and don't share it with
        third parties for commercial purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        Processing is based on the performance of (preparing) a contract with you, or on our
        legitimate interest in responding to questions about Villa Solmira.
      </p>

      <h2>5. How long we keep your data</h2>
      <p>
        Requests that don't lead to a booking are kept for a maximum of [X months]. Data from
        confirmed bookings is kept for as long as legally required for our accounting (usually
        several years). [Exact retention periods to be confirmed.]
      </p>

      <h2>6. Sharing with third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The booking and contact form are processed via <strong>Netlify Forms</strong>, the
        hosting provider of this website (Netlify, Inc., US/EU). Netlify processes the
        submitted data on our behalf, solely to pass it on to us. We don't share your data with
        any other third parties, except where legally required.
      </p>
      <p>
        To display the availability calendar, the site may use a shared Google Calendar. This
        process doesn't involve any personal data of guests — only which periods are booked.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the contact page you can optionally load a map showing the location of Villa
        Solmira (<strong>Google Maps</strong>, Google Ireland Limited). This map only loads
        after you give explicit consent via the cookie banner (the "marketing" category) — see
        "Cookies" below. Once the map is loaded, Google may set its own cookies and process
        technical data under{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Google's privacy policy
        </a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The homepage shows the current temperature, fetched from <strong>Open-Meteo</strong>.
        This service sets no cookies and only receives Villa Solmira's fixed coordinates — no
        personal data about visitors — so it doesn't require consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        With your consent (the "analytics" category) we use <strong>Google Analytics</strong>
        (Google Ireland Limited) to measure how the site is used: which pages are viewed, how
        visitors arrive and whether a request was sent. Google receives technical data such as
        browser, device, approximate location and a random visitor ID; Google Analytics does
        not store IP addresses. The content of submitted forms is not passed on. We don't share
        this data with Google for other purposes or use it for advertising. Without your
        consent, Google Analytics is not loaded.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website uses a cookie banner where you give consent per category. You can adjust
        your preferences at any time via the cookie settings in the site footer.
      </p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Strictly necessary</strong> — always active, no consent required. This
          includes your cookie preference itself and a cookie that remembers which language
          version you chose, so you don't have to pick it again every time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics</strong> — Google Analytics, for visitor statistics (see "Sharing
          with third parties" above). Without your consent in this category, no analytics
          cookies are set.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Marketing</strong> — only the Google Maps embed on the contact page falls
          under this category. Without your consent in this category, that map isn't loaded
          and Google doesn't set any cookies.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>access your data;</li>
        <li>have incorrect data corrected;</li>
        <li>have your data deleted;</li>
        <li>restrict the processing of your data;</li>
        <li>object to the processing;</li>
        <li>receive your data in a portable format.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these rights, contact us at info@villa-solmira.eu. You also have the right
        to lodge a complaint with the competent data protection authority [country / authority
        to be confirmed].
      </p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data against
        loss or unlawful use.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this privacy policy. The date at the top of this page shows when it was
        last updated.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABlock
    title="Questions about your data?"
    text="Feel free to get in touch, we're happy to help."
    ctaLabel="Contact us"
    ctaHref={ROUTES.contact.en}
  />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-intro {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .draft-note {
    background: var(--color-cream-deep);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .legal {
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }

  .legal h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal p {
    color: #3a362c;
  }

  .legal-list {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: #3a362c;
    margin: 0 0 1em;
  }
</style>
